Subject: Cantor Public Procedure Machine Schema Constraint Ledger

@ [ledger_uuid] c17e3a13-6b05-408e-a2db-a95015eb6258

& [HardConstraints] are closed
  + C01 one transport-neutral public form definition per wire subject
  + C02 strict serde and schema derive from or are mechanically checked against the same form
  + C03 canonical dialect is JSON Schema Draft 2020-12
  + C04 every object is closed unless an explicit ordered map is intended
  + C05 required, optional, nullable, and omitted properties match actual serialization
  + C06 enum spellings and tagging match actual serialization
  + C07 integers preserve signedness and exact representable bounds
  + C08 schema object keys and definition order normalize deterministically before digest
  + C09 equal source forms and generator identity produce byte-identical bundles
  + C10 every exported schema has stable id, title, profile, and content digest
  + C11 semantic residuals are explicit and never represented as already proven
  + C12 CLI consumes the shared forms without byte or exit drift
  + C13 provider tool definitions derive from canonical schemas and declare projection loss
  + C14 malformed, unknown, missing, mistagged, out-of-bound, and additional-property fixtures fail schema and serde consistently where expressible
  + C15 schema acceptance never bypasses core semantic validation or admission
  + C16 no network, provider, model, service, persistence, effect, or hardware behavior

& [RiskConstraints] prevent false confidence
  + regex for SemanticId may improve syntax but cannot authenticate identity
  + hex length for digest may improve syntax but cannot establish content correspondence
  + JSON Schema cannot express all cross-field or graph invariants
  + generated schema correctness is tested, not assumed from derive macros
  + provider subset acceptance is not canonical acceptance
  + schema evolution needs explicit compatibility analysis rather than version-string optimism

& [ForbiddenShortcuts] are explicit
  + handwritten deep duplicate schema without drift proof
  + using serde_json Value as an untyped public seam
  + marking additionalProperties true for convenience
  + provider-specific keywords in canonical schema
  + treating tool-call validation as authority admission
  + changing existing base response bytes during form extraction
